{"title":"2019 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Pure_Elementary_Algebra)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Pure Elementary Algebra)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Interactive_Teaching_Approach)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Interactive Teaching Approach)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Claire_Wang_(Timestamp:_25:54)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Claire Wang (Timestamp: 25:54)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the distinct roots of the polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/e/a4ed9bcc72fc4555c3be2fcdcfc2316490cd8fbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3 - 22x^2 + 80x - 67$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"169\" height=\"18\" />. It is given that there exist real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed44e7481e867b959ea84d896b30b222fe5efea3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{1}{s^3 - 22s^2 + 80s - 67} = \\dfrac{A}{s-p} + \\dfrac{B}{s-q} + \\frac{C}{s-r}\\]\" width=\"361\" height=\"41\" />for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/7/917380dced84f6389978d355c92c4e040fea59cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s\\not\\in\\{p,q,r\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/b/3db8f3332a5b70da4d7b3d9db6c0e6b9e73b6164.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac1A+\\tfrac1B+\\tfrac1C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"85\" height=\"21\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/7/0577863302f8209ff40dedef0539f6d1f79bfdfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }243\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }244\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }245\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }246\\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 247$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"444\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Multiplying both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0dd86c1a1143adfa555374b2ac2842cf24edc91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(s-p)(s-q)(s-r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"159\" height=\"18\" /> yields\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/8/98876ccfdf56b419e524f7df285b0d3ec6b34d15.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 = A(s-q)(s-r) + B(s-p)(s-r) + C(s-p)(s-q)\\]\" width=\"440\" height=\"18\" />\nAs this is a polynomial identity, and it is true for infinitely many <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, it must be true for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> (since a polynomial with infinitely many roots must in fact be the constant polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />). This means we can plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/f/1dfc20f5dcffba4a944c9744696cc4ec534cbff4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"11\" /> to find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/3/0d39cc2afcb31489f6bbaf2f61c0fc6fd8cc8877.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac1A = (p-q)(p-r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"149\" height=\"37\" />.  Similarly, we can find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/7/af780f521a40ae8a18a64b2e945fe761c8486068.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac1B = (q-p)(q-r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"153\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/e/ccec7eccb01fea2faa05838cf1e2d5deba6b3737.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac1C = (r-p)(r-q)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"149\" height=\"37\" />.  Summing them up, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/f/b5f6ab443798a3cdbaf34f942a40bb85f346c112.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac1A + \\frac1B + \\frac1C = p^2 + q^2 + r^2 - pq - qr - pr\\]\" width=\"334\" height=\"37\" />\nWe can express <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/c/fbc73e7a1eb614acaadc0056cfd6f34a913bf385.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2 + q^2 + r^2 = (p+q+r)^2 - 2(pq + qr + pr)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"355\" height=\"21\" />, and by Vieta's Formulas, we know that this expression is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/9/3b91c51d372bfcdddb879cc9576495733eaa046c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$484$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />. Vieta's also gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/1/0a1a9a9c52d2da2691c10dbd5cc9ee0f506c06ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pq + qr + pr = 80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"140\" height=\"16\" /> (which we also used to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/e/e2e0c02c63120779ac0d0b254cbdd5a7fb50f1bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2+q^2+r^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" />), so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/0/4908aa23321cdddb0e72e06f0a08c18a01ccbef7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$484 -240 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 244}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"176\" height=\"30\" />. \n</p><p><i>Note</i>: this process of substituting in the 'forbidden' values in the original identity is a standard technique for partial fraction decomposition, as taught in calculus classes.  \n</p><p>-very small latex edit from countmath1&#160;:)\n</p><p>Minor rephrasing for correctness and clarity ~ Technodoggo\n</p><p>-Minor edits by urAntimony\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Pure_Elementary_Algebra.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Pure_Elementary_Algebra)\">Solution 2 (Pure Elementary Algebra)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Pure Elementary Algebra)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Solution 1 uses a trick from Calculus that seemingly contradicts the restriction <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/7/917380dced84f6389978d355c92c4e040fea59cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s\\not\\in\\{p,q,r\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />. Here is a solution with pure elementary algebra.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/2/dc2b5bd2be6d0b72cb01502f5cf150443383b44c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A(s-q)(s-r) + B(s-p)(s-r) + C(s-p)(s-q)=1\\]\" width=\"441\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/2/bc29237ba5c70bcf4308d0310d0b11c0fc47c1a2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[s^2(A+B+C)-s(Aq+Ar+Bp+Br+Cp+Cq)+(Aqr+Bpr+Cpq-1)=0\\]\" width=\"555\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/0/700378ad4f856d1c44923eb7fb2fb6105c556d82.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{cases} A+B+C=0 &amp; (1)\\\\ Aq+Ar+Bp+Br+Cp+Cq=0 &amp; (2)\\\\ Aqr+Bpr+Cpq=1 &amp; (3) \\end{cases}\\]\" width=\"334\" height=\"74\" />\nFrom <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/3/413b90a3858f27557b017b9b2150ee6f6eef5140.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=-(B+C)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/8/0a86a9d0ee572e6cecd91130d332ca4823be30db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=-(A+C)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/e/6becf9eb0bf4c4911e6f37456638446f706ee11c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C=-(A+B)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"20\" />, substituting them in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f62a19f0425d8e6121ca0c1cfd3ce96e43c9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/1/9f174da6d932151a9cf2a3254e0bbb41756df73a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Ap + Bq + Cr=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"18\" />  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/4/104992efa4deaa9a2dfeeec9b331ad0bf628f80a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"25\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/6/0b64bf5cfa5fd85b2910b1a2c74b4ac75c8f7a9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4)- (1) \\cdot r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/d/d3d476bd8f84614c5336b0df4505e009e061ae4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A(p-r)+B(q-r)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"194\" height=\"20\" />  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/7/737a366a904e00f936f8728869ad8f2587dab46f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/f/3ff5321fb065164e334494ca881d517672b225a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3) - (1) \\cdot pq$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/0/d60c22c20615eb2da30f15b8ff99f46cae2ddbeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Aq(r-p)+Bp(r-q)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"212\" height=\"20\" />  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/8/dd8597460a07f59450a07e0f94607fcb479cf974.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/4/ae4502fbcb471642637672ec13edfa007e9582bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6) + (5) \\cdot p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"93\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/f/66feabf1e99359f1122fb03a03ef230f32900e73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A(r-p)(q-p)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"157\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/d/e3d3801778aeaf94c3ccf9750d05764aceac2111.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\frac{1}{(r-p)(q-p)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"152\" height=\"43\" />, by symmetry, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/4/604035be56eb344b219601f92c9c1e9b68b6e593.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = \\frac{1}{(r-q)(p-q)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"153\" height=\"43\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/9/2394f8588c8a64a94b75f915cbe8c239347e46c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = \\frac{1}{(q-r)(p-r)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"152\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>The rest is similar to solution 1, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/0/f603bea74184033e437099194b90135250b18bbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 244}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"75\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~Mathman645: Honestly. this solution isn't even that hard to understand, but the way you factored the initial expression is kinda weird and misleading.\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Isabelchen\">isabelchen</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Interactive_Teaching_Approach.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Interactive_Teaching_Approach)\">Video Solution (Interactive Teaching Approach)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Interactive Teaching Approach)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=33VvJF8fAlc\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=33VvJF8fAlc</a>\n</p><p>~MathkidsbyMax\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GI5d2ZN8gXY\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GI5d2ZN8gXY</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/zw5CCPcT5IU\">https://youtu.be/zw5CCPcT5IU</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Claire_Wang_.28Timestamp:_25:54.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Claire_Wang_(Timestamp:_25:54)\">Video Solution by Claire Wang (Timestamp: 25:54)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Claire Wang (Timestamp: 25:54)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/q-80GjQeWes?t=1554\">https://youtu.be/q-80GjQeWes?t=1554</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A\">2019 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2019 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?ti